 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, three tests are not attributed to the main cause, plus one that is only probably attributed to it. Only the first two are explained with any confidence, and none of the four tracebacks were fully read.\n\n1. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`** fails with a `RuntimeError`. `src/tessel/app.py:1093-1098` raises it when `from asgiref.sync import async_to_sync` fails, because `asgiref` isn't installed. This one is well supported.\n\n2. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`** fails with `AssertionError: assert None...`. The properties in `src/tessel/wrappers.py:60-140` fall back to Werkzeug's `max_content_length`, `max_form_memory_size` and `max_form_parts`, and the base class likely returns `None` instead of the expected defaults. That would also point to an older Werkzeug, so it may share a root cause with the main group, but this is inferred.\n\n3. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`** fails with a truncated pytest-level exception. The source (`src/tessel/app.py:435-436`) should accept mode `\"a\"`, so the cause is unknown and needs the full traceback.\n\n4. **`tests/test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name`** fails with an `AssertionError` and is probably the same cookie `TypeError`, since it goes through `persist_session`. The subagent never saw its traceback, so this is unconfirmed.\n\nI can have the subagent re-run these four with full tracebacks if you want them pinned down.",
